2026-09-01 version 2.1.8-web (current series):
- improvement: your own box now lifts slightly when it is your turn, exactly like the official client; its size ratio next to the opponents follows the 2.1.8 measures, and on phones in portrait the bottom opponent row can no longer touch your box
- improvement: dealer and blind pucks now sit exactly where the official 2.1.8 client puts them - left-column seats carry bet and puck on their left in landscape, the top-centre box splits them (bet right, puck left), the spectator's bottom seat does the same, and with bets inside the box the side puck is centred next to the box
- improvement: bigger, better-placed player boxes on phones, as in the official 2.1.8 client - in portrait the seat rows now adapt to the real box size instead of fixed positions, the community cards fill the free middle band, and the space kept next to the boxes matches your bet display style (less is reserved when bets sit inside the box)
- improvement: the welcome message and server announcements are now translated into your language on every browser - they use the same translation service as the chat and the forum when the built-in browser translator is not available; turning off chat translation also keeps them in their original language
- improvement: the local-backup banner now also appears on a brand-new browser, so you can create your first backup right away
- improvement: the banner offering to restore your settings now explains itself - the browser can keep a local backup of your settings in a folder of your choice, with clear Create / Restore / Later buttons; creating a backup never overwrites an existing backup file
- improvement: the web client now follows the PokerTH 2.1.8 release running on pokerth.net
- improvement: the client now introduces itself to the server as a web client for real - the switch shipped earlier but stayed off until the server could recognise it; web players are now counted as their own client type in server statistics, the Live/Spectator tool and the game-server dashboard
- improvement: the stats HUD on the seats is no longer marked as beta - it is an official feature of the web client, still off by default in Advanced options > Assistance
- improvement: bets are now shown inside the player box by default on phones and tablets too, as in the official client since 2.1.8 - the tray under the box needs no room around the boxes, which suits small screens best. Your own choice in Settings > Styles > Seats, "Bet display", is kept as it is
- new: the Ivoire & Chêne table style - a light oak table with an ivory felt and a brass rail, set in a library, with matching cream buttons and pucks. The first light table of the collection; the chat and log panels follow with a warm parchment tint. Settings > Styles > Table
- improvement: the cards of your deck are loaded in the background when you sit down at a table, so the first hands no longer show blank cards for a moment on mobile networks
- improvement: the assistance win percentage is computed in the background and no longer freezes the table for up to a second on phones after the flop, turn and river; it is also a little more precise
- bugfix: the community cards no longer flicker at the turn and the river - cards already on the board stay put and only the new card flips, as in the desktop client; the river card also no longer showed up before the turn card
- improvement: the table previews in Settings > Styles > Table are the freshly rendered ones from the 2.1.8 desktop client - every table now has a landscape and a portrait preview, showing the bets inside the player boxes, and the default table and Green Casino get a real preview instead of a plain felt crop

2026-08-13 version 2.1.7-web:
