- new: player profiles now show what the desktop client shows - current season rank, score, average, games and points, the last five finishes, placement breakdown with charts, and the cups of all three rankings; the player card and the game info card are ordinary windows you can move and resize, the lobby stays usable behind them
- new: the players list tells you where someone is playing - rest your mouse on a name, or open the card on a phone; server admins get the kickban hammer directly in the list
- new: 90 emoji reactions instead of 30, on three pages you can flip or swipe - faces, hands and party, and a poker page with the shark, the fish, the chicken, the chip rack, a bomb that really explodes and a water pistol that really fires; reactions now reach the table almost instantly
- new: the Disco table style - a seventies club lounge with mirror ball and neon sign - with the Blacklight 4c card deck and the Disco card back to match (upstream 2.1.8 style packs); and the BBC Anthem table theme with its card back (by BaShFX)
- new: choose where bets are shown - in a small tray under the player box (new default on desktop, like the official client) or next to the box as before (default on phones)
- new: bet keypad - on touch devices it opens inside the action bar so nothing jumps around; on computers it floats just above the action bar. The bet slider moves in the same steps as the desktop client and is much easier to use with a finger
- new: the "your turn" notification carries Fold and Check/Call buttons, so you can play a hand from the notification itself
- new: automatic backup - pick a folder once and the app keeps your backup file up to date there, and offers to restore everything in one click if the browser storage was wiped (desktop Chrome, Edge and Opera); the app also asks the browser for persistent storage
- new: open with / share to PokerTH - a style pack, a backup file, a desktop config.xml or an invitation link sent to the installed app is imported or opened on arrival; invitation links open in the app instead of a browser tab
- new: "invite friends" opens a share window - QR code, copy button, whatsapp/telegram/e-mail/sms shortcuts and the phone share sheet; an invite link shows which table you are invited to right on the login screen, and keeps the server address it came from
- new: custom sounds - replace any game sound with your own audio file in advanced options / sound
- new: report an inappropriate avatar from a player's profile - the same report the desktop client sends, available on phones too
- new: five more interface languages - Indonesian, Thai, Filipino, Bengali and Swahili - 45 in total, help included
- new: the poker rules, hand rankings, how-to-play guide, glossary and FAQ pages are now written in all 45 languages, using the same hand names as the game itself; links between them keep your language, right-to-left languages read right to left, and card sequences always read left to right
- new: three pages you can read without opening the app - hand rankings with the odds of each one, a step-by-step how-to-play guide, and a glossary of fifty-five poker terms; sharing a link to them shows a proper preview card
- new: the "suggest players" button in invitation games now also works for BBC and WEC community admins at their community's tables, and lists one player per line; the Monthly Cup templates fill in the real name of the current tournament
- new: session logs - select several logs and delete them in one go, move through the list with the arrow keys
- new: admin page - automatic updates that wait until nobody is connected, weekly reset for the shared leaderboard, music play counts, per-day language chart and "show all" breakdowns on the traffic page, search-engine settings with AI-crawler refusal and IndexNow
- improvement: the web client now introduces itself to the server as its own client type, so server statistics can tell web players apart
- improvement: the app opens from its local copy first and refreshes in the background, downloads updates a few files at a time, and retries a script that failed to load - pages and tables come up instantly even when the server is briefly busy
- improvement: the game proxy protects itself against connection floods - regular play is unaffected
- improvement: the server's inactivity warning is a proper dialog with a countdown, a sound and an OK button
- improvement: chat and private-message translation falls back to a second service when the first one is temporarily blocked (VPN users especially), and tells you when nothing works at all
- improvement: choosing a photo as your avatar is lighter on memory on phones, and your avatar is prepared once when you pick it instead of being re-processed at every sign-in
- bugfix: losing your connection during a running game no longer costs you your seat - the client sits back down at the next hand, within the five minutes the server holds it
- bugfix: a player who walked away from a table kept their seat for ever - seats are now released after the server's inactivity timer, like the desktop client
- bugfix: the lobby could stay on screen with a frozen table list long after the connection had died - the client now notices and reconnects on its own; retries after a refused connection are properly spaced out so the server no longer blocks the address
- bugfix: signing in on pokerth.net stopped working with a "version not supported" error after a server update
- bugfix: "IP address blocked" when two web players joined the same table - the server now sees each player's real address
- bugfix: the "idle players" view no longer lists spectators, and a spectator's status light shows which table they are watching, like the desktop client
- bugfix: the "suggest players" button had gone quiet - the suggestion was swallowed by the chat cleanup; it shows up again, only for you
- bugfix: on iPhone and iPad, the app installed on the home screen opened on a white screen; the player card and the game info card keep clear of the notch and the status bar
- bugfix: the app sometimes offered an update that was already installed, and a newly imported seat pack only showed up after the offline cache renewed itself
- bugfix: the automatic server update could restart in the middle of a game when the only players connected were on phones with the screen off
- bugfix: the All-In button was hard to read on the Green Casino table in light mode; the Monthly Cup link shows the real Monthly Cup badge; the tabs of the About window no longer break words in the middle on phones

